data: {"type":"done","sourceLabel":"DB","sources":[{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #119","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #119","preview":"Question: What is the true form of the Supreme God (Param Akshar Purush)?\nAnswer: God is not a formless energy void. He has a highly defined, majestic"},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #1","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #1","preview":"Question: Who is the ultimate, true Supreme God?\nAnswer: The ultimate Supreme God is Param Akshar Purush, KavirDev (Lord Kabir). He is above the Trini"},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #537","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #537","preview":"Question: Who is the true Supreme God?\nAnswer: KavirDev (Lord Kabir). He is the ultimate creator of the infinite universes, far above Kaal, Brahma, Vi"},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #495","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #495","preview":"Question: Is God formless (Nirakaar) as claimed by many scholars?\nAnswer: This is a grand deception. The Supreme God is not formless; He has a body ma"},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #494","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #494","preview":"Question: Who is the true Supreme God (Purna Brahm) hidden in the Vedas?\nAnswer: The true Supreme God is KavirDev (Lord Kabir). He resides in Satlok ("},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #262","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #262","preview":"Question: Who is the \"Parampita\" (Supreme Father) mentioned in the Bible?\nAnswer: The Bible refers to the Supreme Creator who is separate from the god"},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #713","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #713","preview":"Question: Who is the ultimate Supreme God (Param Akshar Brahm)?\nAnswer: Kabir Saheb."},{"type":"kb","title":"Verified Q&A Bank #781","url":"Verified Q&A Bank #781","preview":"Question: Who is the ultimate Supreme God (Param Akshar Brahm)?\nAnswer: Kabir Saheb."}],"suggestions":["What does the Bible's reference to the Supreme Creator actually mean?","How does Lord Kabir's role as the supreme father relate to other major religious figures?","Can you explain what 'Parampita' exactly refers to in this context?"],"model":"llama-3.3-70b-versatile","chunksUsed":8,"webResultsUsed":0}

